      "requirement": "The usual assumption in the literature is that emissions are proportional to power, that is, if wind contributes 1% of the energy it will reduce emissions by 1%. By this method, PJM estimates Maryland offshore wind will reduce emissions by 0.17 CO 2 /kWh. In reality a little wind saves natural gas, about 0.10lbs CO 2 /kWh. Too much wind can cause base load coal plants to cycle and increase emissions.",
